[2026-03-14T23:06:17.959Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUK2XA5KQmmeD1h8GNr2io","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and start recording (default: about:blank)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings; without IDs, opens interactive menu\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings with details\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings locally\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>`** - Upload source maps for workspaces\n- **`replayio info`** - Show CLI version and browser information\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it for viewing and debugging. Use `replayio upload <id>` if automatic upload doesn't occur after recording completes.\n\nFor advanced debugging integration, install the Replay MCP Server in Claude using the provided configuration command with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac5fa330-6a4d-4ed7-8078-ec8161727750","uuid":"7be87c7f-ac8b-43e6-b30a-4d3219ab5bec","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and start recording (default: about:blank)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings; without IDs, opens interactive menu\n- **`replayio list`** - Display all local recordings with details\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings locally\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps <paths...>`** - Upload source maps for workspaces\n- **`replayio info`** - Show CLI version and browser information\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it for viewing and debugging. Use `replayio upload <id>` if automatic upload doesn't occur after recording completes.\n\nFor advanced debugging integration, install the Replay MCP Server in Claude using the provided configuration command with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.","durationMs":3766,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T23:06:18.209Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Er6CK21LiwzpvjGHFVWXAN","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings—comprehensive captures of browser activity that allow investigation of app behavior like \"a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Concept\nThe recording functions as \"a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed,\" with two fundamental units: **Points** (specific execution moments) and **Elements** (DOM references independent of time).\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened:\n- Error identification (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline views (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding and reading JS files)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why things happened:\n- Dependency tracking showing \"happens-before relationships\"\n- Point details including stack frames and variable values\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Investigation Framework\nThe documentation recommends: frame a question, explore related events, explain causation, form a hypothesis supported by data, then present conclusions with evidence.\n\nA particularly useful technique: \"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac5fa330-6a4d-4ed7-8078-ec8161727750","uuid":"3ca287c6-4433-4a3c-9bcc-790132c8e1c3","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings—comprehensive captures of browser activity that allow investigation of app behavior like \"a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Concept\nThe recording functions as \"a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed,\" with two fundamental units: **Points** (specific execution moments) and **Elements** (DOM references independent of time).\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened:\n- Error identification (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline views (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source inspection (finding and reading JS files)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why things happened:\n- Dependency tracking showing \"happens-before relationships\"\n- Point details including stack frames and variable values\n- Expression evaluation at specific moments\n\n## Investigation Framework\nThe documentation recommends: frame a question, explore related events, explain causation, form a hypothesis supported by data, then present conclusions with evidence.\n\nA particularly useful technique: \"The Logpoint tool is extremely useful for this: see the value of the same expression whenever a statement executed, look for anything unexpected, and continue investigating from there.\"","durationMs":3360,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
